maxDate() computed an approximate upper bound by ceiling the maximum interpolation time to the nearest year and converting back via optionDateFromTenor(Period(..., Years)):

    //FIXME approx
    return optionDateFromTenor(Period((int)ceil(interpolation_.xMax()), Years));

This could over- or under-estimate the true last date by up to a year depending on where in the year the last pillar falls, making extrapolation guards inconsistent with the actual data range.

The curve already stores the input dates in dates_. Returning dates_.back() gives the exact last pillar date with no approximation.
